import type { RawProposal } from './meal-generation'

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE MEAL LIBRARY — original dishes, written for this app (30 Sep 2026).
//
// Ashley asked for hundreds more meals, and chose "write our own, and check
// them" over an open recipe dataset and over copying recipe sites
// (docs/plans/meal-library.md). Nothing here is copied from anywhere: the
// dishes are ordinary ones described in our own words.
//
// WHAT A DISH CARRIES: a slot, a name, a cuisine, a method and its ingredients
// in grams or counts, using only foods the app can cost. NO MACROS. Those are
// worked out per person when a dish is offered, by the same function every
// generated dish goes through, along with the diet check, the dislike filter
// and the scaling to the slot's budget. A dish that suits nobody's numbers is
// never served; the data cannot make the app less safe than a model does.
//
// THE METHOD NAMES NO AMOUNT: the app rescales every dish, and a method that
// says "add 2 tbsp" would contradict the list beside it (the 19 Sep rule).
// "Ready in N minutes" is fine; that is how the quick/standard band is read.
//
// CUISINE LABELS are the app's own (generate-meals' familiar and exotic lists),
// because the pool allows one exotic cuisine per meal and reads tags[0].
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

